@sokra I can reproduce this and have tracked it down to `RealContentHashPlugin.getCompilationHooks(compilation).updateHash.tap`. If I tap into it, like you had suggested at one point, the hash for the file containing the JSON code stays the same between 5.21.2 and 5.24.0, even though the contents changed. If I don't tap into it, the file gets a new hash.

I don't think it's anything in the hook code that would cause this, as that's not modifying any of the data passed in, and it looks like the return value (`oldHash`) is also ignored. What gives?

Ref https://github.com/waysact/webpack-subresource-integrity/blob/cc0bc1a693de206512d06f37319bd7df9a6fdd3d/webpack-subresource-integrity/index.ts#L524-L540
